{
  "title": "Arshad Warsi joins the cast of Shah Rukh Khan's King: Report",
  "publication_date": "2025-04-18T16:36:42+05:30",
  "summary": "Actor Arshad Warsi has been cast in a pivotal role in Shah Rukh Khan's upcoming film 'King', directed by Siddharth Anand. The film marks the big screen debut of SRK's daughter Suhana Khan following her OTT debut in 'The Archies'. While details about Warsi's character remain under wraps, this marks the first major collaboration between the two actors.",
  "content": "Shah Rukh Khan's upcoming film 'King' has been generating significant buzz since its announcement last year. The film is particularly notable as it reunites SRK with Pathaan director Siddharth Anand and marks the theatrical debut of his daughter Suhana Khan, who recently made her OTT debut with The Archies.\n\nAccording to a report by Peeping Moon, Arshad Warsi has joined the cast in a pivotal role, though specific details about his character are being kept confidential. While Shah Rukh Khan and Arshad Warsi have been friends for years, this will be their first significant on-screen collaboration, apart from SRK's previous guest appearance in Warsi's 2005 film 'Kuchh Meetha Ho Jaye'.\n\nThe film is being produced under Khan's Red Chillies Entertainment and Siddharth Anand's Marflix Pictures. The cast also includes notable actors Abhishek Bachchan and Abhay Verma of 'Munjya' fame.",
